;; Seatbelt profile for ck-basal-worker.
;;
;; The worker applies this profile to itself with sandbox_init(3) before it
;; reads its first frame. Everything it needs from then on is already open or
;; mapped: stdin and stdout carry its IPC, stderr carries its logs, and its
;; code and libraries were mapped at launch. So the profile denies everything
;; (files, network, process execution, IPC lookups) and allows only signals
;; to itself, so that an abort inside the engine still terminates the process
;; with SIGABRT where the parent can see it.
;;
;; Reads and writes on descriptors that were open before the profile applied
;; are not file opens, so stdio keeps working.

(version 1)
(deny default)
(allow signal (target self))
